{
  "slug": "barista",
  "name": "Barista",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "barista caffeinates your claude",
  "longDescription": "Keeps a Mac awake while Claude Code works. A **6-trigger hook set** (`UserPromptSubmit`, `PreToolUse` and `PostToolUse` on `Bash`, `Stop`, `StopFailure`, `SessionEnd`) runs `scripts/status.mjs`, which starts `caffeinate` for the session and stops it when the session ends; when background shells are still running when Claude stops, a detached `scripts/watchdog.mjs` keeps `caffeinate` alive until they drain or Claude itself exits. The scripts exit immediately on anything but macOS. MIT.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
